    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Assign multiple bylines to posts, pages, and custom post types via a search-as-you-type input box. Co-authored posts appear on a co-author&#8217;s archive page and in their feed. Co-authors may edit the posts they are associated with, and co-authors who are contributors may only edit posts if they have not been published (as is core behavior).</p>\n<p>Add writers as bylines without creating WordPress user accounts. Simply <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/guest-authors.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">create a guest author profile</a> for the writer and assign the byline as you normally would.</p>\n<p>On the frontend, use the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Co-Authors Plus template tags</a> or the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/blocks.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">block editor blocks</a> to list co-authors anywhere you&#8217;d normally list the author.</p>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<p>Guides for site owners, themers and developers live in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/README.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\"><code>docs/</code> directory on GitHub</a> (they are not bundled in the distribution ZIP):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/guest-authors.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Guest authors</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/roles-and-capabilities.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">roles and capabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Template tags</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/blocks.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">blocks</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/querying-posts.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Querying posts by author or co-author</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/customizing.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Customizing Co-Authors Plus</a>: recipes for the most common filters</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/filters.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Filters and actions</a> and the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/rest-api.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">REST API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/wp-cli.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">WP-CLI commands</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/upgrading-to-4.0.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrading to 4.0</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Co-Authors Plus is an almost complete rewrite of the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/co-authors/\" rel=\"ugc\">Co-Authors</a> plugin originally developed by Weston Ruter (2007). The original plugin was inspired by the &#8216;<a href=\"https://txfx.net/2005/08/16/new-plugin-multiple-authors/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Multiple Authors</a>&#8216; plugin by Mark Jaquith (2005).</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>IMPORTANT: If you are using the original Co-Authors plugin, disable it before installing Co-Authors Plus.</li>\n<li>Extract the co-authors-plus.zip file and upload its contents to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory. Alternately, you can install directly from the Plugin directory within your WordPress Install.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8220;Plugins&#8221; menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Place <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">co-authors template tags</a> in your template.</li>\n<li>Add co-authors to your posts and pages.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<h4>\nHow do I add Co-Authors Plus support to my theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>If you&#8217;ve just installed Co-Authors Plus, you might notice that the bylines are being added in the backend but aren&#8217;t appearing on the front end. You&#8217;ll need to <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">add the template tags to your theme</a> before the bylines will appear.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nWhat happens to posts and pages when I delete a user assigned to a post or page as a co-author?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>When a user is deleted from WordPress, they will be removed from all posts for which they are co-authors. If you reassign their posts to another user, that user will be the co-author instead.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I use Co-Authors Plus with WordPress multisite?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! You can <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/guest-authors.md#multisite\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">use Co-Authors Plus on WordPress multisite</a>. Co-Authors Plus can be activated on a site-by-site basis or network-activated. If you create guest authors, however, those guest authors will exist on a site-by-site basis.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nWho needs permission to do what?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>By default, a WordPress user needs the <code>edit_others_posts</code> capability to assign co-authors to posts, or the equivalent for other post types, such as <code>edit_others_pages</code> for pages. This is typically granted to the Editor role but can be altered with the <code>coauthors_plus_edit_authors</code> filter. The <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/roles-and-capabilities.md#assigning-co-authors\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">roles and capabilities guide</a> has an example that lets the Author role assign co-authors.</p>\n<p>A WordPress user will need the <code>list_users</code> capability to open the Guest Authors screen. This is typically granted to the Administrator role but can be altered with the <code>coauthors_guest_author_manage_cap</code> filter. The <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/roles-and-capabilities.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">roles and capabilities guide</a> covers every permission check in detail.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I easily create a list of all co-authors?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! You can <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md#create-a-list-of-all-co-authors\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">create a list of all co-authors with a template tag</a> <code>coauthors_wp_list_authors()</code> template tag. This template tag accepts many of the same arguments as <code>wp_list_authors()</code>. Look in <code>template-tags.php</code> for more details.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I disable Guest Authors?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! You can disable guest authors entirely through a filter. Having the following line load before <code>init</code> (for example in your theme&#8217;s <code>functions.php</code> or in a plugin) will do the trick:<br />\n    add_filter( &#8216;coauthors_guest_authors_enabled&#8217;, &#8216;__return_false&#8217; )</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I change how bylines and author archives work?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Many parts of Co-Authors Plus can be changed with a filter, for example making every byline come from guest authors, or stopping author archives from matching on the post&#8217;s WordPress author. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/customizing.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Customizing Co-Authors Plus</a> for recipes, and the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/filters.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">filters and actions reference</a> for the full list.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<p>The highlights of recent releases are below. Every change, including older releases, is listed in <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">CHANGELOG.md</a>.</p>\n<h3>4.2.2</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> Guest authors without a linked user no longer receive comment moderation emails, and Contributors no longer receive them for published posts.</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> Co-authors only receive comment emails for posts and comments they can access.</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> Tighten how guest author profiles are looked up, who can see co-authors&#8217; email addresses, how private posts are counted, and who can change a post&#8217;s author.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4.2.1</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> <code>wp co-authors-plus export-coauthors</code> now requires <code>--file</code>. If you ran it without <code>--file</code> on 4.2.0, delete <code>wp-content/cap-coauthors-export.json</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> A Query Loop containing Co-Authors Plus blocks no longer forces &#8220;Reload full page&#8221;.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Author archive URLs for a slug that matches no one return a 404, instead of listing posts.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> The Authors panel and blocks load in the block editor on WordPress 6.4 and 6.5.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Post counts and author lists treat a linked user and guest author as one person, so posts aren&#8217;t counted twice and guest authors don&#8217;t go missing from lists.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Authors whose nicename isn&#8217;t a clean slug, as some SSO and sync plugins write them, appear in the author search and in bylines.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Yoast SEO&#8217;s structured data stays valid on posts with co-authors.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> <code>wp co-authors-plus create-guest-authors</code> accepts <code>--role</code> and other user query arguments again.</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> Tighten how co-authors and author queries are matched.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4.2.0</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> RSS feeds credit each item&#8217;s co-authors on every site. To keep the old feed bylines, return <code>false</code> from the <code>coauthors_filter_feed_authors</code> filter.</li>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> Creating, listing and editing guest authors needs the guest author manage capability (Administrators by default) everywhere, including WordPress&#8217;s own post screens, so Editors can no longer edit guest authors there. Change this with the <code>coauthors_guest_author_manage_cap</code> filter.</li>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> Setting co-authors on pages and custom post types checks that post type&#8217;s own edit-others capability.</li>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> Core&#8217;s <code>/wp/v2/coauthors</code> REST route needs the <code>edit_posts</code> capability, and <code>/wp/v2/guest-author</code> is gone. Read co-authors through the plugin&#8217;s <code>coauthors/v1</code> endpoints, which now return unescaped values.</li>\n<li><strong>Changed:</strong> The plain byline template tags, such as <code>coauthors()</code>, escape their output.</li>\n<li><strong>New:</strong> WP-CLI commands to move guest authors and their bylines between sites (<code>export-coauthors</code>, <code>import-coauthors</code>) and to list a post&#8217;s co-authors (<code>list-authors</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>New:</strong> Filters to change the author data in the editors&#8217; author search, for example to hide email addresses.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Co-author names with apostrophes display correctly in the block editor, and the Authors panel fills in on sites that override the <code>coauthors</code> REST field.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Trashing a guest author no longer drops them from bylines.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed:</strong> Many WP-CLI commands now do what they report, including <code>swap-coauthors --dry-run</code>, <code>reassign-terms</code> and the author term backfills.</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> Tighter permission checks for managing guest authors, and no more user logins in public REST responses.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Assign multiple bylines to posts, pages, and custom post types with a search-as-you-type input box.",
    "description": "<p>Assign multiple bylines to posts, pages, and custom post types via a search-as-you-type input box. Co-authored posts appear on a co-author&#8217;s archive page and in their feed. Co-authors may edit the posts they are associated with, and co-authors who are contributors may only edit posts if they have not been published (as is core behavior).</p>\n<p>Add writers as bylines without creating WordPress user accounts. Simply <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/guest-authors.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">create a guest author profile</a> for the writer and assign the byline as you normally would.</p>\n<p>On the frontend, use the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Co-Authors Plus template tags</a> or the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/blocks.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">block editor blocks</a> to list co-authors anywhere you&#8217;d normally list the author.</p>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<p>Guides for site owners, themers and developers live in the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/README.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\"><code>docs/</code> directory on GitHub</a> (they are not bundled in the distribution ZIP):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/guest-authors.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Guest authors</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/roles-and-capabilities.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">roles and capabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/template-tags.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Template tags</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/blocks.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">blocks</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/querying-posts.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Querying posts by author or co-author</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/customizing.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Customizing Co-Authors Plus</a>: recipes for the most common filters</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/filters.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Filters and actions</a> and the <a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/rest-api.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">REST API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/wp-cli.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">WP-CLI commands</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Automattic/co-authors-plus/blob/main/docs/upgrading-to-4.0.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrading to 4.0</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Co-Authors Plus is an almost complete rewrite of the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/co-authors/\" rel=\"ugc\">Co-Authors</a> plugin originally developed by Weston Ruter (2007). The original plugin was inspired by the &#8216;<a href=\"https://txfx.net/2005/08/16/new-plugin-multiple-authors/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Multiple Authors</a>&#8216; plugin by Mark Jaquith (2005).</p>\n",
